WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:01.230
- Welcome back!

00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:02.580
We've had fun this hour,

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:05.130
but before we go, I have
one last heartwarming story.

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:06.189
This is, What I'm Liking.

00:00:06.189 --> 00:00:09.060
(upbeat music)

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:10.920
Tomorrow is election day, people,

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:12.570
and this next story is a reminder

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:15.750
the American dream is
still alive and well.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:17.640
Estefania recorded her parents

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:20.790
dropping her off at work for
her first day as an attorney,

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:24.030
just like they did when she
was starting school as a kid.

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:25.530
What makes this extra special,

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:27.420
is that she's the first
person in her family

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:29.850
to graduate college and law school.

00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:30.840
Let's get her in here.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.600
Everybody say hi to Estefania.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.469
Watching on NBC Chicago at 3:00.

00:00:35.469 --> 00:00:37.080
(audience applause)

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:37.995
Hello!

00:00:37.995 --> 00:00:39.150
- Hello.

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:40.980
Thank you so much for having me.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:43.260
- No, thank you so much for being awesome!

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:44.640
We're so excited to highlight.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:46.560
So your parents, they seemed so proud.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:47.910
So tell us about them.

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:50.115
- Yes, so I grew up in Chicago.

00:00:50.115 --> 00:00:53.550
My parents immigrated
here from Tarabu, Mexico

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:54.960
before I was born.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:57.870
My parents have been
extremely present in my life.

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:00.030
They would take any time off of work

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:02.070
to be at every single one of my events.

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:05.160
Whether it was academic
or extra curriculars,

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:06.198
they were there.

00:01:06.198 --> 00:01:08.280
Starting from a very young age,

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:10.230
they reinforced that education

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:12.690
was the route to success in this country.

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:15.305
I watched them sacrifice and work so hard

00:01:15.305 --> 00:01:17.580
so that I could be successful.

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:19.110
- Aw, that's incredible.

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:20.460
Why do you think so many people

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:23.370
have responded the way
they have to this video?

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:26.829
- I think achieving a goal
with a foundation of hard work,

00:01:26.829 --> 00:01:30.000
sacrifice and love for your people

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.100
really just resonated with everyone

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:35.280
and that's especially true
with the Latino community.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:38.790
It's a reminder that the
American dream isn't dead.

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:40.890
There's an entire generation of immigrants

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:43.320
and children of immigrants like myself,

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:44.550
who are breaking barriers

00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:46.140
and becoming widely successful

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:48.030
in their respective career paths,

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:49.495
and then on top of it,

00:01:49.495 --> 00:01:53.580
Latinas in law is a huge focus of mine.

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:57.005
Latinos make up just 2%
of the legal profession,

00:01:57.005 --> 00:02:01.740
but Latinos make up 19% of
our population at this point.

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:03.390
It's time that the percentage grew

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:07.200
to reflect our population
as a whole in this country.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:09.060
- Absolutely!

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:10.920
Well, way to get the ball rollin', mam.

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:12.240
Congratulations.

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:13.350
We're all super proud of you.

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:14.430
Thanks Estefania.

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:16.119
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:16.119 --> 00:02:18.090
(audience applause)

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:19.080
And that's not all,

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:21.690
our season long partner
Pilot pen makers of Frixion,

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:23.940
the go to pen of the Kelly Clarkson show,

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:27.240
want to truly honor unstoppable
people just like you, mam,

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:29.940
so they're going to be writing
you a check for $1,000.

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:30.773
You deserve it.

00:02:32.407 --> 00:02:33.869
- Thank you so much.

00:02:33.869 --> 00:02:34.702
- No, absolutely.

00:02:34.702 --> 00:02:35.670
You deserve it.

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:37.800
Congratulations,

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:39.600
and thank you to all our guests this hour.

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:42.330
Angela Bassett, Raymond
Lee, Lindsey Stirling,

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:43.320
and Chem Teacher Phil.

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:44.160
Y'all have a great day,

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:46.210
and if it's not great, try and change it.

